<title>PERU: Nestle paid $67 mln for D'Onofrio - stockbroker.</title>
<headline>Nestle paid $67 mln for D'Onofrio - stockbroker.</headline>
<dateline>LIMA 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Switzerland's Nestle SA paid $67 million for its recent purchase of a 98.7 percent stake in Peru's largest ice-cream and confectionery company D'Onofrio, a stockbroker close to the deal said on Thursday.</p>
<p>He said Nestle paid $0.88 per share, while an official at the Lima Stocks and Securities Board (CONASEV) confirmed that a total of 76 million shares were sold in the deal.</p>
<p>The price of the sale, which was concluded earlier this month after a year of negotiations, has not been publicly disclosed.</p>
<p>((-- Marco Aquino, Lima newsroom, 511 221-2134))</p>
